    "introduction": "Lloyds Banking Group provides financial services primarily to customers in the UK through brands including Lloyds Bank, Halifax, Bank of Scotland and Scottish Widows. Its activities span current accounts, savings, mortgages, consumer credit, business banking, insurance, pensions and investments. The group earns interest from lending and fees from financial services, supported by a large deposit base. Its domestic focus connects performance closely with UK household finances, housing activity and business conditions. Mortgage pricing, deposit competition and credit losses influence earnings, while digital banking and branch services support customer relationships. Insurance and retirement products add longer-term financial relationships alongside its core banking operations.",
